{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01422",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 7.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Doctor, I've checked them in and done the preliminary measurements, I'll hand them over when you ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.94,
      "end_seconds": 14.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.57,
      "end_seconds": 25.52,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come. She's been having been losing weight without trying, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.69,
      "end_seconds": 31.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.85,
      "end_seconds": 37.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Since this morning, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.42,
      "end_seconds": 47.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Okay, so and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 47.18,
      "end_seconds": 53.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, uh, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.14,
      "end_seconds": 60.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "I, I was getting to that! I've also had drenching night sweats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.75,
      "end_seconds": 64.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.82,
      "end_seconds": 67.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.78,
      "end_seconds": 71.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Have you had a cough that won't go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.29,
      "end_seconds": 78.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "So, um, yes, about the same, about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.08,
      "end_seconds": 95.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.38,
      "end_seconds": 100.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I'm on omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 102.02,
      "end_seconds": 110.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "Ah, she is supposed to take it once a day, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.86,
      "end_seconds": 113.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Paracetamol, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.09,
      "end_seconds": 117.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.98,
      "end_seconds": 120.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "650 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.62,
      "end_seconds": 124.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "How long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.24,
      "end_seconds": 130.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "About three months now. Diclofenac I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.16,
      "end_seconds": 133.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.81,
      "end_seconds": 138.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.4,
      "end_seconds": 156.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.89,
      "end_seconds": 162.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I'm allergic to diclofenac, I get wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.87,
      "end_seconds": 167.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.82,
      "end_seconds": 174.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol. My father had bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.57,
      "end_seconds": 179.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.36,
      "end_seconds": 207.89,
      "duration_seconds": 27.53,
      "text": "Let me think, I have acid reflux, for five years. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. My family kept telling me to get it checked. Okay, so yes, arthritis in my knees. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.55,
      "end_seconds": 216.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Alright, arthritis in your knees, that matches what I have here. Any sign of fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.08,
      "end_seconds": 219.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.21,
      "end_seconds": 225.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "A few quick ones: chest pain or bone pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.15,
      "end_seconds": 230.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "I mean, no, no chest pain or bone pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.24,
      "end_seconds": 237.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Alright, any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.47,
      "end_seconds": 240.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.5,
      "end_seconds": 244.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.62,
      "end_seconds": 248.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Mm, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 250.69,
      "end_seconds": 262.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.79,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 15, saturation 98 percent, heart rate 78, blood pressure 112 over 74, temperature is 36.7 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.91,
      "end_seconds": 265.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.33,
      "end_seconds": 270.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.66,
      "end_seconds": 273.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.39,
      "end_seconds": 294.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "There is a firm, painless lump in the left side of your neck about three centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.71,
      "end_seconds": 327.3,
      "duration_seconds": 29.59,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with symptoms that need an urgent cancer work-up. Another possibility is a lymphoma. I'll request an ultrasound of the neck, it'll help with neck lump. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'll request blood tests, it'll help with weight loss. I am referring you on an urgent pathway, which means an appointment within two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.98,
      "end_seconds": 346.25,
      "duration_seconds": 18.27,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. Please come and see me after the scans. Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.99,
      "end_seconds": 354.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "So, um, I come back after the scans. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.84,
      "end_seconds": 360.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.72,
      "end_seconds": 364.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}